WEBVTT

00:03.160 --> 00:05.900
Go, Eren!

00:14.150 --> 00:15.760
In the year 850...

00:16.610 --> 00:18.680
For the first time,

00:18.680 --> 00:21.840
humanity recovered part of its 
territory from the Titans.

00:23.220 --> 00:25.530
Though at great cost.

00:28.050 --> 00:33.300
Then I welcome everyone 
here to the Survey Corps!

00:33.700 --> 00:35.640
This is a true salute!

00:36.010 --> 00:37.390
Offer up your hearts!

00:39.260 --> 00:40.320
Yes, sir!

00:44.430 --> 00:46.660
You have done well to endure your fear.

00:47.480 --> 00:49.570
You are brave soldiers.

00:50.310 --> 00:51.980
You have my heartfelt respect.

00:53.690 --> 00:54.990
A month later,

00:55.750 --> 00:59.040
led by Erwin Smith, the Survey Corps left Karanes

00:59.040 --> 01:01.490
to find a route to Zhiganshina,

01:01.490 --> 01:06.540
where it's believed the secrets 
of the Titans are held.

01:12.110 --> 01:15.300
We will now begin the 57th 
expedition beyond the walls!

01:16.390 --> 01:18.140
Onward!

02:51.020 --> 02:55.980
Female Titan 
57th Expedition Beyond the Walls (1)

03:16.060 --> 03:18.380
Ahead, to the left, a 10-meter class!

03:18.750 --> 03:22.260
I am very interested in seeing 
what's inside its stomach...

03:22.990 --> 03:24.760
But I'll leave it to the support team!

03:28.130 --> 03:28.890
Damn!

03:29.350 --> 03:30.390
Not deep enough.

03:31.180 --> 03:32.900
Defend the formation!

03:37.150 --> 03:38.440
Stay strong!

03:38.640 --> 03:40.830
Leave it to the support team, and keep going!

03:43.110 --> 03:46.950
Onward! Onward!

03:52.030 --> 03:54.960
The support teams will only 
accompany us to the old city area.

03:55.310 --> 03:58.400
Once we're past that, 
it's completely Titan territory.

03:58.800 --> 04:04.220
The long-range scouting formation devised 
by Commander Erwin is our only hope.

04:04.920 --> 04:07.610
We, the special ops squad, are here.

04:10.230 --> 04:12.260
Sir, can they...

04:13.020 --> 04:15.150
Can my classmates beat the Titans?

04:15.570 --> 04:16.520
Huh?

04:16.520 --> 04:19.670
What have you been doing the past month?

04:20.990 --> 04:22.940
Listen, brat...

04:22.940 --> 04:24.700
The most crucial part

04:24.700 --> 04:27.320
of an expedition is in how 
you avoid fighting Titans—

04:35.720 --> 04:38.170
Go into long-range scouting formation!

04:40.220 --> 04:41.680
See ya, Armin.

04:42.480 --> 04:45.050
If you run into a Titan, don't piss your pants!

04:45.610 --> 04:46.640
Right!

04:46.640 --> 04:47.780
Same to you, Jean.

04:55.290 --> 04:56.800
Row 3-3: Relay

04:55.730 --> 04:57.340
The vanguard is to spread out in a semi-circle.

04:57.340 --> 05:00.980
But stay within visual range of one another.

04:58.790 --> 05:00.310
Row 5-Center: Standby

05:00.980 --> 05:02.780
Position yourselves at fixed intervals.

05:01.800 --> 05:03.310
Row 2-5: Relay

05:03.530 --> 05:07.590
Extend the recon and message relay 
range as far as possible.

05:04.300 --> 05:06.060
Row 3-4: Relay

05:07.180 --> 05:09.860
Row 2-4: Relay

05:33.240 --> 05:34.280
We'll be fine...

05:34.590 --> 05:35.610
Calm down!

05:40.060 --> 05:44.660
It's primarily the forward recon squad 
that will encounter Titans.

05:45.710 --> 05:47.540
Row 1-8: Recon

05:51.160 --> 05:55.700
As soon as one is sighted, 
they'll fire a red smoke round.

05:58.860 --> 06:03.110
Anyone who sees the flare should fire 
the same round to relay the signal.

06:04.470 --> 06:06.390
Row 2-Center: Command

06:06.940 --> 06:10.180
When the Commander sees it,

06:10.180 --> 06:12.140
he'll fire a green smoke round,

06:13.670 --> 06:16.770
and show the formation where to go.

06:18.770 --> 06:23.520
Thus, the entire formation can advance

06:23.520 --> 06:25.860
toward the goal, while avoiding Titans.

06:26.260 --> 06:28.170
Row 2-3: Relay

06:28.640 --> 06:32.990
But sometimes, due to terrain or obstacles,

06:32.990 --> 06:36.120
a Titan won't be sighted until 
it's within the formation.

06:42.890 --> 06:44.460
Red... Red...

06:44.460 --> 06:45.920
Red smoke round...

06:50.120 --> 06:51.800
Blause! Over here!

06:54.190 --> 06:56.670
Damn it! Did we let one through?

06:56.670 --> 06:58.060
We'll draw it this way.

06:58.570 --> 07:00.440
Blause, get over here!

07:11.260 --> 07:12.240
I'll handle it!

07:12.240 --> 07:13.190
Split off!

07:13.190 --> 07:14.160
Yes, sir!

07:32.460 --> 07:33.720
Sir...

07:33.720 --> 07:35.010
Back into position!

07:35.280 --> 07:36.770
He ran out of gas.

07:42.020 --> 07:43.610
Something's wrong...

07:43.940 --> 07:46.370
It's been a while since we saw the red smoke round,

07:46.370 --> 07:47.980
but they still haven't reformed.

07:48.470 --> 07:49.490
It can't be...

07:50.690 --> 07:53.910
Note that this strategy only works on normal Titans,

07:53.910 --> 07:57.240
whose behavior can be easily predicted.

08:00.160 --> 08:01.660
A black smoke round?

08:02.290 --> 08:04.010
Is a Titan ignoring the nearby humans

08:04.010 --> 08:06.210
and heading for the formation's center?

08:06.960 --> 08:08.000
It has to be...

08:08.450 --> 08:09.590
That's

08:10.880 --> 08:12.190
an Aberrant!

08:13.870 --> 08:16.850
It's only necessary to fight Aberrants,

08:16.850 --> 08:18.510
whose behavior is unpredictable.

08:18.510 --> 08:21.100
Damn, we'll have to fight it...

08:21.100 --> 08:22.940
Sys, go for the neck!

08:23.480 --> 08:24.900
I'll stop it!

08:24.900 --> 08:26.230
Roger!

08:28.130 --> 08:31.320
Using Maneuver Gear on flat 
terrain is a huge disadvantage.

08:31.320 --> 08:33.320
It almost never works.

08:33.680 --> 08:36.480
But I can't let it disrupt the formation.

08:37.350 --> 08:39.980
I think that's Arlert over there.

08:39.980 --> 08:42.810
I don't want one of the 
new guys to run into it.

08:43.210 --> 08:44.370
We kill it here!

08:52.950 --> 08:54.130
Now, Sys!

09:01.140 --> 09:03.270
You did it, Squad Leader Ness!

09:06.030 --> 09:07.190
Did I get him?

09:09.110 --> 09:10.430
You came for me?

09:10.430 --> 09:12.370
That's my partner...

09:13.210 --> 09:15.670
I love you, Shallot!

09:23.970 --> 09:24.990
Again?

09:25.370 --> 09:27.960
What is the right flank recon squad doing?

09:27.960 --> 09:29.870
If it ignored them and came this way,

09:29.870 --> 09:31.620
it must be another Aberrant.

09:32.490 --> 09:33.940
Oh, fine...

09:35.080 --> 09:37.010
Sys, we do it again.

09:37.010 --> 09:37.800
Right.

09:38.760 --> 09:42.310
But we've got the worst luck, 
doing this twice in a row...

09:42.860 --> 09:45.370
And I think it's at least a fourteen-meter class.

09:45.720 --> 09:47.390
This one will be tough.

09:57.000 --> 09:58.210
What's that?

09:58.210 --> 09:59.370
It's too fast!

09:59.570 --> 10:01.330
Don't let it reach Arlert!

10:01.330 --> 10:02.030
Sys!

10:02.530 --> 10:03.570
Right!

10:37.950 --> 10:40.280
No... No.

10:40.740 --> 10:41.920
That's no Aberrant.

10:42.270 --> 10:43.620
It's intelligent!

10:44.040 --> 10:46.850
Like the Armored or Colossal Titans, or Eren...

10:47.450 --> 10:49.830
A human in the body of a Titan!

10:50.370 --> 10:51.330
B-But who?

10:51.920 --> 10:52.840
Why?

10:53.320 --> 10:54.800
This is bad! What should I do?

10:54.960 --> 10:55.970
I'm going to die, too...

10:55.970 --> 10:56.880
I'll be killed!

10:58.610 --> 11:00.380
Go! Run!

11:07.870 --> 11:09.310
What does it...

11:11.580 --> 11:13.810
No, what do they...

11:17.110 --> 11:18.980
What do they want?

11:20.950 --> 11:26.080
<b>Information We Can Share So Far:</b>

11:20.950 --> 11:26.080
<b>Long-Range Scouting Formation (1) 
Devised by Survey Corps Commander 
Erwin Smith, its use has dramatically 
increased survival rates outside the walls.</b>

11:26.080 --> 11:31.080
<b>Information We Can Share So Far:</b>

11:26.080 --> 11:31.080
<b>Long Range Scouting Formation (2) 
Put simply, it's a form of human "radar." By quickly 
alerting Erwin in the center to the discovery of 
any Titans, the Survey Corps can change course.</b>

11:33.420 --> 11:35.250
Someone tell them...

11:36.150 --> 11:40.170
That the right flank recon squad 
has been wiped out...

11:40.850 --> 11:45.450
A Female Titan brought 
a huge Titan army!

11:47.030 --> 11:49.560
Is anyone there?

12:47.900 --> 12:50.160
It's not going to kill me?

12:50.620 --> 12:51.840
Why?

12:53.040 --> 12:55.040
It removed my hood...

12:55.420 --> 12:59.740
To... To look at my face?

13:00.430 --> 13:01.310
Armin!

13:02.520 --> 13:03.570
Reiner!

13:04.440 --> 13:06.300
Hey, can you stand?

13:06.840 --> 13:11.390
You won't last outside the walls 
unless you're on horseback...

13:11.390 --> 13:12.390
Hurry!

13:12.390 --> 13:13.430
Right!

13:15.670 --> 13:18.320
I saw the smoke round signaling an Aberrant.

13:18.320 --> 13:20.770
Was it that one there with the nice ass?

13:20.770 --> 13:22.350
That's no Aberrant...

13:22.350 --> 13:24.400
It's a human in a Titan body!

13:24.720 --> 13:25.900
What was that?

13:27.010 --> 13:28.170
Wait a second.

13:28.170 --> 13:29.700
We need to fire a smoke round first.

13:30.060 --> 13:31.300
H-Hurry...

13:31.550 --> 13:33.350
There's an emergency over there.

13:33.830 --> 13:34.870
With a smoke round, I'll...

13:36.010 --> 13:39.130
Wait... I think Jean fired it.

13:42.170 --> 13:44.240
It came from the right flank.

13:44.240 --> 13:47.090
Does that mean we're so compromised, 
we can't continue the mission?

13:47.550 --> 13:50.390
Looks like the right flank recon 
squad was partially wiped out...

13:50.390 --> 13:52.480
Titans, tons of them.

13:52.480 --> 13:53.720
I don't know why,

13:54.380 --> 13:56.850
but there are lots of fast ones.

13:56.850 --> 13:58.660
For now, we're holding them back,

13:58.660 --> 14:00.560
but recon is no longer possible...

14:01.000 --> 14:02.670
We've taken heavy losses,

14:02.670 --> 14:04.300
and if we aren't careful, we'll be destroyed!

14:05.040 --> 14:07.110
That Titan came from the same direction.

14:07.670 --> 14:08.530
No way...

14:09.030 --> 14:11.210
Was it leading the Titans?

14:11.620 --> 14:12.830
It?

14:13.440 --> 14:15.830
Why is a Titan over there?

14:16.370 --> 14:17.300
An Aberrant?

14:17.620 --> 14:23.300
No, it's a human in a Titan body...

14:23.300 --> 14:25.420
Someone with the same ability as Eren.

14:25.790 --> 14:27.170
What?

14:27.480 --> 14:29.860
Why do you think that, Armin?

14:31.080 --> 14:33.640
The Titans only eat us.

14:34.070 --> 14:36.320
We're just killed in the process.

14:36.320 --> 14:38.600
Killing us isn't ever specifically their goal.

14:39.090 --> 14:41.860
But when Sys aimed for its weak spot,

14:42.400 --> 14:45.320
it crushed him and smashed him into the ground.

14:46.830 --> 14:50.140
It killed him to kill, rather than to eat him.

14:50.580 --> 14:52.870
Its nature is different from the others.

14:53.530 --> 14:57.430
When the Colossal and Armored 
Titans destroyed the walls,

14:57.430 --> 15:01.130
it must've been the one that 
brought that army of Titans.

15:01.730 --> 15:04.930
Their goal has consistently been to attack all humanity!

15:06.680 --> 15:08.380
No, maybe not.

15:08.980 --> 15:11.520
It felt like it was looking for someone...

15:12.000 --> 15:14.770
If that is the case, 
could it be looking for...

15:15.710 --> 15:17.560
Could it be looking for Eren?

15:17.930 --> 15:19.600
Eren?

15:19.600 --> 15:24.100
Eren's with Squad Levi, which is 
in charge of the right flank.

15:24.750 --> 15:26.030
The right flank?

15:26.660 --> 15:30.670
The plans I got had them 
to the rear of the left flank.

15:31.850 --> 15:36.600
Mine said they were near 
the front of the right...

15:37.060 --> 15:40.040
Wait, there's no way they'd 
be on the front lines.

15:40.440 --> 15:42.920
So where are they?

15:43.370 --> 15:46.600
Probably the safest place in the formation.

15:47.680 --> 15:51.590
Which means in the center, 
and toward the rear...

15:52.220 --> 15:53.050
Armin!

15:53.410 --> 15:55.810
There's no time to think.

15:56.080 --> 15:59.310
Smoke rounds can't possibly indicate 
how much of a threat it poses!

15:59.900 --> 16:02.330
At this rate, it'll wipe out command.

16:02.330 --> 16:05.540
Then the formation will fall apart, 
and that'll be the end.

16:05.540 --> 16:06.900
What are you trying to say?

16:07.310 --> 16:08.760
In other words,

16:08.760 --> 16:11.630
at this range, we may still be 
able to draw its attention.

16:12.160 --> 16:15.350
We may be able to buy time to withdraw.

16:15.910 --> 16:19.080
Maybe... Maybe...

16:21.280 --> 16:23.790
But it really is intelligent.

16:24.090 --> 16:27.750
To it, we are nothing but insignificant insects.

16:27.750 --> 16:29.840
It'll just crush us...

16:30.160 --> 16:31.360
Seriously?

16:32.770 --> 16:34.340
That's scary...

16:34.630 --> 16:37.630
Hey, are you really Jean?

16:37.630 --> 16:41.850
The Jean I know never thinks 
of anyone but himself.

16:42.520 --> 16:44.390
Don't be an ass...

16:46.440 --> 16:51.150
I just don't want those charred bones I saw

16:51.640 --> 16:53.640
to be disappointed in me!

16:54.090 --> 16:56.440
I...

16:57.010 --> 16:59.840
I know what I have to do now!

17:00.180 --> 17:03.100
And this is the job we chose.

17:03.100 --> 17:04.290
Help me!

17:09.980 --> 17:11.490
Put on your hood.

17:11.490 --> 17:12.610
As far forward as you can...

17:12.610 --> 17:14.630
So that your face is hidden from it.

17:14.970 --> 17:19.580
I don't think it will kill us until 
it knows who we are!

17:19.580 --> 17:20.760
Oh...

17:21.210 --> 17:24.570
You believe if it thinks we might 
be Eren, it won't kill us?

17:25.030 --> 17:27.150
If nothing else, it'll make me feel better.

17:27.150 --> 17:30.270
Let's just hope it has poor eyesight!

17:31.080 --> 17:36.510
Armin, I thought it was creepy 
how you always clung to Eren.

17:36.950 --> 17:38.620
But I've always thought you had it in you.

17:39.850 --> 17:41.370
Uh, thanks.

17:41.910 --> 17:44.620
But "creepy"? That's really mean...

17:59.390 --> 18:01.970
It's going much more slowly 
than when I first saw it.

18:02.390 --> 18:03.530
Is it tired?

18:04.330 --> 18:06.950
If it runs at that speed again, we'll be too late!

18:07.340 --> 18:10.190
Now's our chance... We have to do it now!

18:16.340 --> 18:19.320
Listen up... Remember what I said.

18:19.710 --> 18:22.200
Try to draw its attention 
for as long as possible,

18:22.200 --> 18:24.570
to give the formation time to withdraw!

18:24.570 --> 18:26.780
Keep it here as long as you can.

18:27.610 --> 18:30.730
If we could cut its Achilles tendon, 
that'd be more than enough.

18:31.050 --> 18:33.650
But don't do anything stupid...

18:33.650 --> 18:35.050
Don't try to kill it!

18:35.550 --> 18:38.280
It's aware of the weak spot on its neck.

18:38.650 --> 18:41.050
It's totally different than other Titans...

18:41.050 --> 18:42.640
It is impossible to kill.

18:43.070 --> 18:47.270
At least, not by any normal human being.

18:50.660 --> 18:51.630
However...

18:51.630 --> 18:53.890
If it's those two... Maybe...

19:35.670 --> 19:36.530
Armin!

19:38.860 --> 19:40.010
This one...

19:40.010 --> 19:42.310
Its movements are much more 
precise than the others' are!

19:42.310 --> 19:43.400
Damn it.

19:43.400 --> 19:44.490
I...

19:44.770 --> 19:46.660
I underestimated it!

19:51.860 --> 19:53.630
It protected its neck...

19:53.900 --> 19:54.590
Jean!

19:56.190 --> 19:58.460
Damn it! I can't get away!

19:58.800 --> 19:59.720
I'm going to die!

20:00.240 --> 20:02.090
Once it grasps my wire, it's over!

20:05.810 --> 20:06.820
Jean!

20:06.820 --> 20:09.810
Avenge the suicidal bastard!

20:11.320 --> 20:12.310
Armin?

20:13.340 --> 20:15.010
It stopped?

20:15.560 --> 20:16.590
That's the one...

20:16.590 --> 20:18.340
That's the one that killed him!

20:18.340 --> 20:21.140
He rushed to his death on the right flank!

20:21.140 --> 20:23.530
Avenge him!

20:29.130 --> 20:30.250
What happened?

20:31.580 --> 20:33.600
Did Armin hit his head and go insane?

20:33.600 --> 20:35.320
This isn't the time...

20:37.310 --> 20:38.250
R-Reiner?

20:39.120 --> 20:41.970
It crushed my best friend!

20:42.230 --> 20:44.930
I saw his body under its foot!

20:47.800 --> 20:49.810
He's going straight for the neck?

20:50.000 --> 20:51.480
No, it's working!

20:51.480 --> 20:54.150
While it's distracted by Armin!

21:02.030 --> 21:03.860
H-Hey...

21:17.040 --> 21:20.480
H-Hey... Reiner, you...

21:37.410 --> 21:39.650
Reiner did it!

21:39.980 --> 21:42.310
Mikasa was so strong, I forgot.

21:42.310 --> 21:45.490
But he's really strong and reliable, too...

21:46.320 --> 21:48.420
We've bought enough time, right?

21:48.420 --> 21:50.080
Let's get the hell away from it!

21:50.680 --> 21:54.330
If it isn't a man-eater, it won't follow us!

22:02.740 --> 22:03.790
Look...

22:03.790 --> 22:08.090
That big bitch got scared 
and decided to go home!

22:09.430 --> 22:10.930
No... Why?

22:11.610 --> 22:13.670
That's toward the center rear.

22:14.240 --> 22:15.250
Is it

22:15.670 --> 22:17.390
heading toward Eren?

23:53.410 --> 23:55.160
"You monster..."

23:55.660 --> 23:57.660
Even highly trained members of the Survey Corps

23:57.660 --> 24:00.370
are unable to stop the Female Titan.

24:01.110 --> 24:08.220
The monster finally catches sight 
of Eren in a forest of giant trees.

24:05.460 --> 24:08.310
Forest of Giant Trees 
57th Expedition Beyond the Walls(2)
